  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>e4127a4972ea702a852d4ec34e56d937</srcmd5>
    <version>3.12.3</version>
    <time>1786026114</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-aiofile to 3.12.3.

DEPENDS ON SR 1369632 (python-caio 0.12.2) -- please stage the two together.
aiofile 3.12.0 raised its requirement to caio~=0.12.0, so this package now
Requires python-caio &gt;= 0.12.0 and Factory still carries caio 0.11.1. Accepting
this one on its own would leave python3NN-aiofile unresolvable until the caio
request lands.

Upstream changes since 3.11.1:
- 3.12.1 fixes a double close() and a TextFileWrapper.read() that could read
  past the requested length, and adds a 'closed' attribute
- 3.12.0 bumped the caio dependency to ~=0.12.0
- 3.12.2 and 3.12.3 are a throughput benchmark and README updates

Packaging: the dependency floor moves from 0.9.0 to 0.12.0 to match upstream,
and the licence file is now installed with %license -- it was not packaged at
all before.

Verified locally on aarch64/openSUSE_Tumbleweed against caio 0.12.2 from
devel:languages:python: build green, rpmlint 0 errors 0 warnings, spec-cleaner
diff empty, source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1369634</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
